WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.425
Dependency risks begin with visibility.

2
00:00:02.425 --> 00:00:11.564
Teams need to know what components are used, where they run, who owns them, and whether they affect systems that process, store, or transmit CUI.

3
00:00:11.564 --> 00:00:17.731
Unsupported software becomes difficult to defend because security fixes may no longer be available.

4
00:00:17.731 --> 00:00:25.254
End-of-life frameworks, plugins, runtimes, and operating systems should be replaced or isolated according to risk.

5
00:00:25.254 --> 00:00:31.899
Third-party components and supply chain dependencies can introduce vulnerabilities or malicious behavior.

6
00:00:31.899 --> 00:00:38.654
Package sources, build tools, container images, and vendor software should be governed as part of the application boundary.

7
00:00:38.654 --> 00:00:44.172
Vulnerability response requires prioritization, testing, and timely remediation.

8
00:00:44.172 --> 00:00:52.653
Teams should evaluate exploitability, exposure, compensating controls, and business impact while avoiding indefinite patch delays.

9
00:00:52.653 --> 00:00:55.536
Maintain software inventory and ownership.

10
00:00:55.536 --> 00:00:58.789
Use dependency scanning and vulnerability monitoring.

11
00:00:58.789 --> 00:01:03.329
Patch, upgrade, replace, or isolate vulnerable components.

12
00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:06.852
